                        Ami-Express door support
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

LogicBBS supports Ami-Express doors. Most doors that do not touch specific
internal data files used by /X, and only uses calls/functions through the
ports do most likely run 100% on LogicBBS.

We had a few undocumented commands, so if you do meet problems using a
specific door you can send us this utility and with explanation, how to
install it and what seems to be the problem using it.
Before you do this, make sure you have tested it, using some kind af "snoop"
tool, so you can see that the door don't look for files / configs used by /X.

If /X tool programmers have problems running their doors with LogicBBS, and
they want us to make it compatible with LogicBBS. They must contact us and
tell us what went wrong and how we can support the "call" that did not work.

File listings utilities can easily be made compatible creating the NDIRS file.
But then sysops must avoid the NAMEDIR command used in the conference filebase
setup.


NOTE: This is not an emulation, and performance of /X doors are exactly as
      when used with /X or better.
                           (As you know this is made in first class assembly,
                            NOT third class 'C')

Ports supported:    AEDoorPortX
                    AeServer

These ports are normally called through the amix.library. or directly by
a programmer.
